        "text": "ADVANCED 6/9: ASYNC AND LATENT FLOWS\nA latent node SUSPENDS the exec chain and resumes it later, without blocking the game. Delay and\nRetriggerable Delay are nodes; `wait::frames` is a native. Timers (`timer::set`) are the other\ntool: they raise the engine event `TimerFired(timer)` instead of suspending a chain.\nRule of thumb: Delay for a one-off sequence, Timer for anything that repeats or must be cancelled.",
        "position": [
          0,
          -290
        ],
        "size": [
          1500,
          190
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.75,
          0.2,
          0.28
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "1. DELAY CHAIN - three Delay nodes (milliseconds) space out the countdown logs; each Delay's\n`Completed` wire continues one second later while the game keeps running. A Delay ignores new\ntriggers while it is counting down. After \"go!\" a LOOPING timer is started (every 2 s) and its\nid stored: `timer::set` returns an i64 handle used to match events and to cancel.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          -70
        ],
        "size": [
          3380,
          250
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.45,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "bp",
          "cd_log0",
          "cd_delay0",
          "cd_log1",
          "cd_delay1",
          "cd_log2",
          "cd_delay2",
          "cd_go",
          "cd_timer",
          "cd_store"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "2. TIMER EVENT - `On TimerFired` reports WHICH timer elapsed (`timer` id). Compare it with the id we\nstored so other timers on the object are ignored. Count a heartbeat, log it, and after three\nstop the timer with `timer::clear`. Without clearing, a looping timer runs forever.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          620
        ],
        "size": [
          3720,
          500
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "tf",
          "tf_id",
          "tf_mine",
          "tf_if",
          "tf_beats",
          "tf_inc",
          "tf_set",
          "tf_cat",
          "tf_log",
          "tf_enough",
          "tf_if2",
          "tf_clear",
          "tf_stop"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-4",
        "text": "3. DEBOUNCE - Retriggerable Delay restarts its countdown on every trigger, so the log only appears 500 ms\nafter the LAST space press (typing, charging an attack, saving after edits). A plain Delay would\nignore later presses; this one extends the wait instead.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          1540
        ],
        "size": [
          2360,
          480
        ],
        "color": [
          0.6,
          0.35,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "kd",
          "kd_space",
          "kd_if",
          "kd_n",
          "kd_inc",
          "kd_set",
          "kd_wait",
          "kd_log"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-5",
        "text": "4. WAITING FRAMES - a custom event can also be latent. `wait::frames(count)` suspends the event's chain for\nthat many ticks (`wait::next_tick` for one). Useful for hit flashes and \"let physics settle\" steps.\nbegin_play starts it by dispatching the custom event; a second begin_play node is fine: all\nbegin_play nodes run, one after another.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          2460
        ],
        "size": [
          1340,
          520
        ],
        "color": [
          0.8,
          0.3,
          0.3,
          0.22
        ],
